// Minimal stub node for the policy CI fixture. The Cedar policy engine binds to
// graph ids + branches, not schema content, so a one-node schema is enough to
// materialize the three representative graphs (memory / code_example / bridge)
// that policy validate + policy test run against. NOT the production schema —
// that lives in ../schema/schema.pg and witan-code's code-schema.pg.
node Node {
  slug: String @key
}
